# FROST network device configuration
#

config NET_VENDOR_FROST
	bool "FROST devices"
	default y
	help
	  If you have a network device belonging to the FROST RISC-V SoC,
	  say Y.

	  Note that the answer to this question doesn't directly affect the
	  kernel: saying N will just cause the configurator to skip all
	  the questions about FROST devices.

if NET_VENDOR_FROST

config FROST_NET10G
	tristate "FROST net10g 10GBASE-R Ethernet"
	depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM && HAS_DMA
	help
	  Driver for the 10GBASE-R Ethernet controller of the FROST SoC: a
	  soft MAC/PCS with RX and TX descriptor rings in system memory
	  and one interrupt.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here. The module
	  will be called frost_net10g.

endif # NET_VENDOR_FROST
